The **2007–2008 financial crisis** , or **Global Economic Crisis** ( **GEC**
), was the most severe worldwide [ economic crisis ](/wiki/Financial_crisis
"Financial crisis") since the [ Great Depression ](/wiki/Great_Depression
"Great Depression") . [ Predatory lending ](/wiki/Predatory_lending "Predatory
lending") in the form of [ subprime mortgages ](/wiki/Subprime_lending
"Subprime lending") targeting low-income homebuyers,  [1]  excessive risk-
taking by global [ financial institutions ](/wiki/Financial_institution
"Financial institution") ,  [2]  a continuous buildup of [ toxic assets
](/wiki/Toxic_asset "Toxic asset") within banks, and the bursting of the [
United States housing bubble ](/wiki/2000s_United_States_housing_bubble "2000s
United States housing bubble") culminated in a " [ perfect storm
](/wiki/Perfect_storm "Perfect storm") ", which led to the [ Great Recession
](/wiki/Great_Recession "Great Recession") .

