* There exists two random variables  X  ∼  ρ  ,  Y  ∼  ν  {\displaystyle X\sim \rho ,Y\sim \nu }  ![{\\displaystyle X\\sim \\rho ,Y\\sim \\nu }](https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/2bb317085e8759794c6a07ab363f8e4949d5da0d) , such that  X  =  Y  \+  δ  {\displaystyle X=Y+\delta }  ![{\\displaystyle X=Y+\\delta }](https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/7f05a07df948c65e0de960b0d16373054167283b) , where  δ  ≥  0  {\displaystyle \delta \geq 0}  ![{\\displaystyle \\delta \\geq 0}](https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/1cdd05219dad5f088e59d0964159ef1fb12d7ad4) .

